# AIDE SESSION

Cold-start protocol for agents reorienting on this project. This is a
snapshot of the current architectural intent and the anti-regression
invariants every build phase must hold. It is NOT historical commentary —
superseded design decisions are cut, not annotated.

## State summary (set 2026-10-25, v0.12.0 released — awaiting restart)

v0.12.0 is released. The feature commit is 2421374, the release commit de56e49, the tag v0.12.0; Publish and CI are green and npm serves 0.12.0. The published dist/versions.json has 46 artifacts, including docs/changelog and agents/aide/aide-upgrader, and the package ships CHANGELOG.md. The global install is @aidemd-mcp/server 0.12.0. The registration plans (root package.json files, initContent registry with the aide-upgrader agent and the changelog doc from the root CHANGELOG.md, installAgents/installMethodologyDocs tests, the buildVersionsMeta release gate) were built and QA passed with no todo. Before release the full suite was 2871 green twice, tsc clean, build OK. The aidemd.dev sync is BLOCKED: the headless `claude -p` in the site folder failed with 'Not logged in · Please run /login'. The user must log the CLI in, then rerun the sync. The site's files were not hand-edited. The plans, todo lists and briefs are still on disk, untracked and uncommitted; they close after the restart, through the real aide_frontmatter.

Task `let-session-aide-exist-without-a-linked-kanban-task` (In Progress), with the P1 bug `aide-scaffold-overwrites-existing-files` folded in (In Progress). The user redesigned the feature on 2026-10-25. The session record is a working file like a plan or todo list, not methodology, so it comes from aide_scaffold. aide_scaffold gets type "session" (always .aide/session.aide), and its blank template is the one source of the placeholder. aide_scaffold never overwrites any file of any type. aide_init tells the agent to call aide_scaffold type=session instead of writing the file itself, and /aide boot calls the same tool when the file is missing. aide_cleanup removes a plan/todo/brief only when it is fully checked OR carries `status: abandoned` in the file. The agent sets that mark only after the user discards the work. The rule is per file, an abandoned plan takes its brief, and allowEmptyPlan is removed. The earlier three aide_init plans (methodology-category seed step) were discarded and, with the user's OK, shell-deleted once, because aide_cleanup can't remove unbuilt plans yet. Specs amended and approved: src/tools/scaffold/.aide, src/tools/cleanup/.aide, src/service/install/.aide.

This repo's stray `.aide/versions.json` (`{}`) came from the cli/init integration tests running a real init in the repo. That's fixed (see above), and a full test run no longer creates it.

